	(text "NIBBLE CARD CTR1 - COUNTER BIT 1: program counter bit 1 and return register bit 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a01a1cc3-5e02-4b9e-a62c-c5f53182bc16")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  62 transistors, 34 resistors, 2 LEDs, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nFrom the bus header: PCE (count), PCL (load the jump target), CLK, RST.   To the bus header: PC1.\nFrom the sequencer over the LINK ribbon (2x6, chained along the eight counter cards): OPR1 (the jump target bit), PCR (load the return address), RAI (save the return address).\nCount carry TC1 in from bit 0 over the IN link; TC2 = TC1 and PC1 out to bit 2 over the OUT link.\nPC1: a master-slave flip-flop whose input is PC xor carry (count, or hold when PCE is low), OPR1 (PCL) or RA1 (PCR).  RA1: a transparent latch open while RAI and PH1.  RST clears both.\ndocs/isa.md is the specification; sim/emu.py the reference the whole-machine simulation checks the cards against."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d298a9ef-ddb6-42b1-b5f8-b88e405b1b7d")
	)
	(text "TWO-PHASE CLOCK and RSTN (as on the register and sequencer boards)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ae96edbb-05e9-4f1d-8878-8490ab32a5e7")
	)
